# Review: follows architecture

Read `doc/architecture.rst` before judging layer, thread, blackboard,
device, or HTTP changes. Do not invent a parallel architecture.

## Layers

Foundation (`util/`, `Math/`, `Geo/`, `io/`) → Engine → Backend
(`Device/`, `Computer/`, `Blackboard/`) → UI. Lower layers must not
include headers from higher ones.

## Reject

- Device drivers or CalculationThread including `Dialogs/`, `Form/`,
  `Widget/`, or calling `CommonInterface` / `ActionInterface`
- UI thread using `DeviceBlackboard`; draw thread using
  `InterfaceBlackboard`; network/asio thread calling UI APIs
- Putting a type in the wrong layer to avoid a dependency
- Blocking HTTP on the UI thread; long-lived HTTP without
  `Net::AsyncTask` and `NetComponents::BeginShutdown()`
- Dialogs or message boxes from Backend (use
  `InputEvents::processGlideComputer` or `UI::Notify`)

```cpp
// BAD: driver shows UI
#include "Dialogs/Message.hpp"
ShowMessageBox(_("IGC failed"), ...);

// GOOD: queue a glide-computer event; UI thread handles it
InputEvents::processGlideComputer(GCE_...);
```

Details: `.cursor/rules/xcsoar-project-rules.mdc` (Architectural Layers,
Blackboard, Backend→UI Event Queue).
